"""
The public path representation used by `std::path` and `std::fs`.

`Path` owns its backing `Buffer` through the `erg storage` field. The buffer
contains raw POSIX bytes when `platform` is `PathPlatform.Posix`, or raw
target-endian UTF-16 code-unit bytes when it is `PathPlatform.Windows`.
`length` excludes the trailing null terminator and `capacity` is the backing
buffer capacity. Callers must construct paths through the validated factory
verbs rather than manufacturing inconsistent metadata.
"""
open struct Path {
    """Owned raw path storage; the `erg` owner drops it with the path."""
    erg storage: Buffer,
    """Platform discriminator selecting POSIX bytes or Windows UTF-16 units."""
    erg platform: PathPlatform,
    """Logical payload length; the trailing null terminator is excluded."""
    erg length: Int,
    """Total storage capacity available to the owned path."""
    erg capacity: Int,
    """One when storage ends with the required platform null terminator."""
    erg terminated: Int,
}

"""
Identifies the raw path representation and platform separator contract.

The discriminator is metadata only; it never converts bytes to UTF-8 or
converts UTF-16 code units to a string. `Posix` stores arbitrary non-null
bytes. `Windows` stores validated UTF-16 code units in the target ABI layout.
"""
open enum PathPlatform {
    """POSIX path bytes using `/` as the root and separator character."""
    Posix,
    """Windows UTF-16 code units using drive and UNC root rules."""
    Windows,
}
